<p>Notes: All share data restated to reflect two-for-one stock split effective March 20, 1997.</p>
<p>1996 results include two non-recurring charges totalling $0.24 a share.</p>
<p>As part of its recapitalization strategy folowing the sale of its water operations, in September 1966, the company defeased the $28.7 million outstanding principal amount of its 10.125 percent senior notes and recorded an extraordinary loss of $1.1 million, or $0.11 a share, net of income taxes. In additiion, during 1996, the company's utility subsidiary, PG Energy Inc, repurchased a portion of its preferred stock. The premium paid on these repurchases resulted ina charge of $0.13 a share.</p>
<p>Full company name is Pennsylvania Enterprises Inc.</p>
